# Ubuntu for Xiaomi Pad 8 Pro $release_name

Ubuntu 26.04 Desktop ARM64 for Xiaomi Pad 8 Pro, dual-booting alongside Android. $summary_en

## Changes

$updates_en

## Get, install and upgrade

[Fresh installation]($repo_url/blob/$release_name/docs/INSTALL.md) · [Upgrade an existing installation]($repo_url/blob/$release_name/docs/UPGRADE.md) · [Build guide]($repo_url/blob/$release_name/docs/BUILD.md) · [Kernel source]($kernel_url/tree/$release_name)

Attachments include `$prefix-boot.zip` boot images, `$prefix-tools.zip` switching and recovery tools, `$prefix-packages.zip` upgrade packages, and split system image files. Download every image part, concatenate them in filename order and decompress, and verify with `SHA256SUMS.assets`. Existing users should install the complete `packages.zip` set and reboot, retaining the previous kernel and rollback boot set. Installation erases Android data; read [README Before Installing]($repo_url/blob/$release_name/README.md#️-read-before-installing) first.

## Known limitations

$limits_en

Kernel: Linux $kernel_version; stock baseline: `$stock_build` (slot A). Full hardware support is listed in the [README hardware support table]($repo_url/blob/$release_name/README.md#hardware-support).

Sources and licensing: see [README acknowledgments and licensing]($repo_url/blob/$release_name/README.md#acknowledgments-and-licensing); the maintenance image's BusyBox $busybox_version source is available as an [Ubuntu source package](https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/busybox/$busybox_version).
